*** Settings ***
Documentation
...                  == Purpose ==
...                  This file contains the keywords to interfacte to the TTI multiple analysis library written in python.
...
...                  == Description ==
...                  This library is used to analyze a TTI trace content from a JSON format file.
...                  Events are managed in separated dataframes
...                  It is an interface to a python lib available in python/TtiTrace SWENG folder.
...
...                  *Main keywords:*
...                      -    Create Tti Multi Analyzer: This keyword is used to create the Tti Multi Analyzer object
...                      -    Verify Distribution Table Of: This keyword is used to verify the distribution table of the data
...                      -    Check Min Max Doesnt Exceed: This keyword is used to check if the min and max values of the data don't
...                                                        exceed the limits
...                      -    Get Column Values: This keyword is used to get the values of the given column
...                      -    CCheck Substrings In Columns: This keyword is used to check the multi columns values given as a dictionary
...                      -    Check Multi Columns Values: This keyword is used to check the multi columns values given as a dictionary
...                      -    Check Value Inrange For Column: This keyword is used to check all the values are in the range for the given
...                                                           column
...                      -    Check Value Inrange For Column Dict: This keyword is used to check all the values are in the range for the
...                      -    Export Dataframes To CSV: This keyword is used to export the current dataframe to a CSV file
...                      -    Export Dataframes To JSON: This keyword is used to export the current dataframe to a CSV file
...                      -    Apply analyzer Method To Event List: This keyword is used to apply an analyzer method to the given event list
...
...                  == Usage ==
...                  The Multi Tti Analyzer object is created using the Create Tti Multi Analyzer keyword
...                  the KW getting information are usuful to analyze the data content and quality
...                  The TtiAnalysisInterface library can be used to analyze the TTI data if some keywords is not available in this library
...
...                  == Example ==
...                  | Create Tti Multi Analyzer | ${path_to_json} | ${list_events} |
...                  | Verify Distribution Table Of | ${column_name} | ${plot}=None | ${validate}=None | ${need_return}=False |
...                  | Check Min Max Doesnt Exceed | ${column_name} |
...                  | Get Column Values | ${column} |
...                  | Check Substrings In Columns | ${substrings} |
...                  | Check Multi Columns Values | ${column_value_dict} |
...                  | Check Value Inrange For Column | ${column} | ${range} |
...                  | Check Value Inrange For Column Dict | ${column_range_dict} |
...                  | Export Dataframes To CSV | ${path_to_csv} |
...                  | Export Dataframes To JSON | ${path_to_csv} |
...                  | Apply analyzer Method To Event List | ${method} |
...
...
...                  Some files robotframework and in python are given as examples in
...                        examples folder
...                        and python/Examples folder
...

Library            ../python/TtiTrace/MultipleTtiAnalysis.py


*** Keywords ***

Create Tti Multi Analyzer
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to create the Tti Multi Analyzer object.
    ...                A JSON file containing a TTI trace is mandatory for the keyword.
    ...                This file can be generated by converting a pcap capture file using
    ...                the TtiConvert library.
    ...                The Tti Multi Analyzer object is used to analyze the TTI data with
    ...                each event managed in separated dataframes.
    [Arguments]    ${path_to_json}    ${list_events}
    ${my_instance} =    Make_myClass    ${path_to_json}    ${list_events}
    [Return]    ${my_instance}

Verify Distribution Table Of
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to verify the distribution table of the TTI data.
    ...                The distribution table is used to check the distribution of the data. A graph included in an HTML page is generated.
    [Arguments]    ${column_name}    ${plot}=None    ${validate}=None    ${need_return}=False
    ${result_df} =    TtiAnalysis.Verify Distribution Table Of    ${column_name}    ${plot}    ${validate}    ${need_return}
    [Return]    ${result_df}

Check Min Max Doesnt Exceed
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to check if the min and max values of the data don't exceed the limits.
    [Arguments]    ${column_name}
    ${result} =    Apply analyzer Method To Event List    ${column_name}
    [Return]    ${result}

Get Column Values
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to get the values of the given column.
    [Arguments]    ${column}
    ${values_list} =    Apply analyzer Method To Event List    ${column}
    [Return]    ${values_list}

Check Substrings In Columns
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to check the substrings in the columns.
    ...                The substrings are given as a list.
    ...                The keyword returns a dictionary with substrings as keys and lists of columns containing the substring as values.
    [Arguments]    ${substrings}
    ${substr_dict} =    Apply analyzer Method To Event List   ${substrings}
    [Return]    ${substr_dict}

Check Multi Columns Values
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to check the multi columns values given as a dictionary.
    ...                The dictionary contains the column name as the key and the value as the value.
    ...                The keyword checks if the given values are present in the columns.
    [Arguments]    ${column_value_dict}
    ${result} =    Apply analyzer Method To Event List   ${column_value_dict}
    [Return]    ${result}

Check Value Inrange For Column
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to check all the values are in the range for the given column.
    [Arguments]    ${column}    ${range}
    ${result} =    Apply analyzer Method To Event List    ${column}    ${range}
    [Return]    ${result}

Check Value Inrange For Column Dict
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to check all the values are in the range for the given columns.
    ...                The columns and the ranges are given as a dictionary.
    [Arguments]    ${column_range_dict}
    ${result} =    Apply analyzer Method To Event List   ${column_range_dict}
    [Return]    ${result}

Export Dataframes To CSV
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to export the current dataframes to some CSV files.
    ...                The CSV files are saved in the same folder as the origin JSON file.
    ${result} =    MultipleTtiAnalysis.Save Tocsv For All Events
    [Return]    ${result}

Export Dataframes To JSON
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to export the current dataframe to some JSON files.
    ...                The JSON files are saved in the same folder as the origin JSON file.
    ${result} =    MultipleTtiAnalysis.Save Tojson For All Events
    [Return]    ${result}

Apply analyzer Method To Event List
    [Documentation]    This keyword is used to apply the analyzer method to the event list.
    ...                The method name is given as an argument.
    ...                The method returns a dict of results, one for each event.
    ...                In the response dict keys are the event names.
    [Arguments]    ${method}
    ${result} =    MultipleTtiAnalysis.Apply Analyzer Method To Event List    ${method}
    [Return]    ${result}
